say what a file to string conversion detected and produced

An application that reads a file and shows nothing has either got no bytes, or bytes it could not
decode, and a nil string looks the same to it as an empty file. This prints byte count, the encoding
DETECTION answered, the encoding actually used and the resulting length, in one line.

Detection answering 0 falls back to NonLossyASCII, which is a guess rather than an answer, so the
detected value is printed separately from the used one.

ALSO A LATENT USE AFTER FREE, introduced and caught in the same sitting and worth saying out loud:
the copy path frees bytes before returning, so a trace at the end may not read them again. The
detection result is captured into its own variable BEFORE the fallback and the free, which is why
_NSDetectEncodingOfBytes is now called once rather than twice.

MEASURED ON iA WRITER and the answer was ZERO calls. This path is never taken, so whatever the
application uses to turn Cider.md into text, it is not initWithContentsOfURL:usedEncoding:.

BOTH CONTROLS RUN, because a silent probe proves nothing on its own: CIDER_TRACE_TEXT was demonstrably
on in that run (871 TEXTEDIT lines, 23 TEXTDRAW, 346 TEXTFIT), and the string CIDER_TEXTREAD is
present in the built Foundation binary.

--- a/src/NSString.m
+++ b/src/NSString.m
@@ -1095,7 +1095,8 @@
 
 - (id)_initWithBytesOfUnknownEncoding:(void *)bytes length:(NSUInteger)length copy:(BOOL)shouldCopy usedEncoding:(NSStringEncoding *)usedEncoding
 {
-    NSStringEncoding encoding = _NSDetectEncodingOfBytes(bytes, length);
+    NSStringEncoding detected = _NSDetectEncodingOfBytes(bytes, length);
+    NSStringEncoding encoding = detected;
 
     if (encoding == 0)
     {
@@ -1107,16 +1108,31 @@
     {
         *usedEncoding = encoding;
     }
+    id result;
     if (shouldCopy)
     {
-        id string = [self initWithBytes:bytes length:length encoding:encoding];
+        result = [self initWithBytes:bytes length:length encoding:encoding];
         free(bytes);
-        return string;
     }
     else
     {
-        return [self initWithBytesNoCopy:bytes length:length encoding:encoding freeWhenDone:YES];
+        result = [self initWithBytesNoCopy:bytes length:length encoding:encoding freeWhenDone:YES];
     }
+
+    /* THE WHOLE FILE TO STRING CONVERSION IN ONE LINE. An application that reads a file and shows
+     * nothing has either got no bytes, or bytes it could not decode, and a nil here looks the same
+     * to it as an empty file. Detection answering 0 falls back to NonLossyASCII above, which is a
+     * guess, so print what was DETECTED as well as what came out. Task #194.
+     *
+     * bytes is freed above on the copy path, so nothing here may read it again. */
+    if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_TEXT") != NULL && getenv("CIDER_TRACE_TEXT")[0] != (char) 0)
+    {
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_TEXTREAD bytes=%lu detected=%lu used=%lu -> %s length=%lu\n",
+                (unsigned long) length, (unsigned long) detected, (unsigned long) encoding,
+                result != nil ? "string" : "NIL", (unsigned long) [result length]);
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
+    return result;
 }
 
 - (id)_initWithDataOfUnknownEncoding:(NSData *)data
